Wording attack (engine trace, engine/stepper.go + engine/month.go):
Guardrails.Evaluate runs only at monthInYear==0, including m=0 (the very
first month). At m=0, CumulativeInflation is still 1.0 (compounding is
gated `if m>0`), and NewGuardrailState seeds PeakPortfolio=InitialPortfolio
=starting PortfolioValue, so year-0's GuardrailCutTrigger/RaiseTrigger are
literally starting_portfolio*(1-drop%) / *(1+rise%) — computed at t=0, in
today's dollars by construction (nominal==real at that exact instant).
month.go's finalizeCurrentYear/currentYearSummary assignment (with the
comment "constant within a year ... last month's assignment wins") confirms
year-0's stored trigger is this same value throughout the year. So "Next
yearly check: cut if the portfolio falls below $X" is accurate: X is
established today and is what the NEXT yearly boundary (month 12) tests
against. This does not collide with GV2's chart-summary "Next cut if..."
line (projection-chart.html, sourced from the LAST year's summary, always
qualified "(future dollars; today: ...)") — different card, different year,
explicit disambiguation.

